Given:

Coordinates of point F = (22, 52)

Coordinates of point C = (18, 44)

Formula Used:

Distance between two points (x₁, y₁) and (x₂, y₂) is sqrt{(x₂-x₁)² + (y₂-y₁)²} 

Calculations:

Let F = (x₂, y₂) = (22, 52)

Let C = (x1, y1) = (18, 44)

Distance FC = sqrt{(22-18)² + (52-44)²}

⇒ Distance FC = sqrt{(4)² + (8)²}

⇒ Distance FC = sqrt{16 + 64} 

⇒ Distance FC = sqrt{80}

The distance between F and C is sqrt{80} unit.
